From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jairo Valdivia <valdiviaprado.ing@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:46:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: surface_charger: Fix positive return value in
 spwr_ac_get_property()

spwr_ac_update_unlocked() returns 1 when ac->state changes, 0 when
unchanged, and a negative errno on failure. Checking if (status) in
spwr_ac_get_property() causes the first property read observing a state
transition (such as initial registration when AC is connected) to abort
without populating val->intval and return +1 to power_supply_sysfs.

Check for status < 0 and normalize status to 0 before reading the
requested property.

Fixes: e61ffb344591 ("power: supply: Add AC driver for Surface Aggregator Module")
Signed-off-by: Jairo Valdivia <valdiviaprado.ing@gmail.com>
Patchset: surface-sam
Link: https://github.com/linux-surface/kernel/pull/184
---
 drivers/power/supply/surface_charger.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/surface_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/surface_charger.c
index d4bba6b41..6346cdf7a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/surface_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/surface_charger.c
@@ -145,8 +145,9 @@ static int spwr_ac_get_property(struct power_supply *psy, enum power_supply_prop
 	mutex_lock(&ac->lock);
 
 	status = spwr_ac_update_unlocked(ac);
-	if (status)
+	if (status < 0)
 		goto out;
+	status = 0;
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE:
